1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E05 -= Superdad =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:01:05,851 --> 00:01:08,063
-麦克! -救命
- Mike! - Help.

3
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,260
-麦克，把这疯狗带走 -救命
- Mike, get that rabid animal out of here. - Help.

4
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,820
爸爸，斯图不是疯狗 那叫活泼
Come on, Dad. Stuart's not rabid. He's peppy.

5
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:19,680
吃人的动物不能用“活泼”来形容
Mike, animals that live off human toes are not "peppy."

6
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,100
这下算了.
This is great.

7
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,820
我要帮帮不在家的邻居，做点好事.
I mean, I'm trying to do a good deed for a neighbor who's out of town...

8
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:25,240
你们抱怨什么？
and all you guys can do is complain.

9
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,880
你怎么只会对这样走路的人做好事
How come you only do good deeds for neighbors who walk like this?

10
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:35,980
你懂不懂“善有善报”这句话？
Ben, does the phrase "one good turn deserves another" mean anything to you?

11
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:38,840
麦克，你懂不懂.
Mike, does the phrase "get that dog out of here...

12
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,900
“把狗带走，否则格杀勿论”这句话？
"before I punt it through the greenhouse" mean anything to you?

13
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,040
嗨，凯罗
Hi, Carol.

14
00:01:48,561 --> 00:01:49,932
嗨
Hi.

15
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,620
怎么了？
What's the matter, Carol?

16
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,320
我找不到花生酱
I cant find the peanut butter.

17
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,040
妈妈什么时候回家？
When's Mom coming home?

18
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:04,740
往常一样
Usual time.

19
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,960
可以打电话给她吗？
Can I call her at work?

20
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,520
若有急事，当然可以
Course you can, sweetheart. If it's important.

21
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,800
请问麦姬.西弗在吗？
Yeah, is Maggie Seaver there, please?

22
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:21,460
让她回来后打给凯罗，急事
Yeah, could you tell her to call Carol when she gets back? It's really important.

23
00:02:23,829 --> 00:02:25,220
好的
Okay.

24
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:26,040
谢谢，再见
Thanks. Bye.

25
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:30,220
有话要对我说吗？
Something you want to talk to me about?

26
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:31,460
不知道.
I don't know.

27
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,140
我需要离开吗？
Want me to leave you alone?

28
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:36,760
不知道.
I don't know.

29
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:41,100
我需要扮小坏弹琴.
Do you want me to stick large ripe vegetables in my ear...

30
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,040
来逗逗你吗？
and play the accordion?

31
00:02:45,484 --> 00:02:48,920
别这样，记得你小时候.
Hey, come on. Remember what we used to do when you we're just a little girl...

32
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:49,660
有困难时会怎样？
and you had a problem?

33
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:53,000
我会推你过来，哔哔 转过身.
I'd steer you over here, beep-beep, spin you around...

34
00:02:53,192 --> 00:02:56,373
抱你上来
and up on the counter like that...

35
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:59,960
接着我们面对面谈
so that we could have a little face-to-face chat.

36
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,120
-是的 -现在行不通了
- Yeah. - Doesn't work anymore.

37
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:08,040
来，跟我谈谈
Come on, talk to me.

38
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:13,840
今天是德国小组出售玩具熊最后一天
Today was the last day of the German Club Gummy Bear sale and...

39
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:18,500
也是让凯文注意到我的最后机会
well, that was my last real chance to get Kevin to notice me...

40
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,920
明天就要举行舞会
before the dance tomorrow night.

41
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:23,540
凯文的朋友马克过来买玩具熊
And Kevin's friend Mark was coming up to get a Gummy...

42
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,925
玛丽莎说她听到马克说他说.
and Melissa said she heard Mark said he said--

43
00:03:25,925 --> 00:03:27,796
等等，谁说的？
Wait, wait. Who said?

44
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,540
-凯文说的 -说什么？
- Kevin said. - Said what?

45
00:03:30,663 --> 00:03:32,238
说.
Said....

46
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,900
说我像一只玩具熊
Said I look like a Gummy Bear.

47
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,840
亲爱的，他这话是善意的
Well, honey, I'm sure he meant it in a nice way.

48
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:45,020
算了吧，他认为我是一只胖熊
Come off it, Dad. I mean, the boy thinks I look like a bear.

49
00:03:45,978 --> 00:03:47,580
是我坏陋
I'm just ugly.

50
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:49,720
你不像一只胖熊
You do not look like a bear.

51
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:53,620
但如果老是认为自己坏
But if you walk around thinking that you...

52
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:56,820
长大后就会变成这样，瞧
look ugly, then you're going to end up looking like this. Look.

53
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,360
看见自己了吗？
Can you see yourself?

54
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:07,380
如果认为自己漂亮.
Now if you walk around knowing you're pretty...

55
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,620
因为你确实漂亮
because you are...

56
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,580
那么心情就会好，长大后会变成这样
then you're gonna feel better. You're gonna look like this.

57
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,020
你怎么看？
What do you think?

58
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:21,420
重要的是凯文怎么看
I think it's more important what Kevin thinks.

59
00:04:22,481 --> 00:04:24,090
好.
Okay...

60
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:26,440
你亲耳听到凯文说.
but did you actually hear Kevin say...

61
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:28,420
他觉得你像一只玩具熊吗？
that he thought you looked like a Gummy Bear?

62
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,300
没有，但玛丽莎说听见了
No, but Melissa said she heard he said it.

63
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:35,800
你相信玛丽莎的每一句话？
Well, since when did you believe everything Melissa says she heard?

64
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:39,280
她有时候确实让人怀疑
Well, she does make you wonder sometimes.

65
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:43,480
她还发誓说在JC百货看到明星了
I mean, she swore she saw Mick Jagger at JC Penney's last week.

66
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,480
那里的家具确实大减价
Well, they did have that big sale in Home Furnishings.

67
00:04:49,041 --> 00:04:50,480
爸爸
Dad.

68
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,700
拜托，我认为.
Come on, I just think that...

69
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:56,280
你应该区分“听说凯文说的话”和.
you should take your cues about what Kevin thinks...

70
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:57,980
“凯文亲口说的话”
from what Kevin says himself.

71
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:01,240
你说得对
Yeah, you're right.

72
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:04,280
我要买溜冰鞋
I need new ice skates.

73
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:07,800
我听错了？
Did I miss something?

74
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:12,240
明晚大家都会去溜冰
Well, everybody's going to be at the skating rink tomorrow night...

75
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,800
我会靠近凯文，听听他会说什么
and I can skate by Kevin and see if he says anything to me.

76
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:19,840
我们明早去商店.
Tomorrow morning you and I go down to Macy's...

77
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,560
买一双新的溜冰鞋
and we buy you a brand-new pair of skates.

78
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,860
也许能在商店碰到明星呢
Who knows, maybe well even run into Tina Turner in Small Appliances.

79
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:28,920
爸爸，谢谢
Thanks, Dad.

80
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:32,625
凯罗
Carol.

81
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:38,380
-凯罗 -妈妈，我在这
- Carol. - I'm in here, Mom.

82
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:43,880
-上当了？ -是啊
- Fooled you, didn't l? - Yeah.

83
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,040
甜心
Hi, sweetheart.

84
00:05:45,531 --> 00:05:48,360
凯罗呢？我收到留言说她找我
Wheres Carol? I got a message that she wanted to talk to me.

85
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:50,420
她去劳莉家了，你今天好吗？
She's over at Laurie's. How was your day?

86
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,500
又要临时改稿
Another last-minute rewrite.

87
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:55,740
平生首次打字这么快 手指现在还在跳呢
I've never typed so fast in my life. My fingers are still wiggling.

88
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,120
那就别浪费了
Don't be wasting those wiggling fingers.

89
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,540
来，帮我揉揉肩膀
Here, try them right here below the shoulder blade.

90
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:00,800
杰森
Oh, Jason.

91
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,440
很好，谢了
Perfect. Thank you.

92
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:08,340
凯罗要谈什么？ 吉姆说她很伤心
So what did Carol want to talk about? Jim said she sounded very upset.

93
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:12,180
她说凯文有可能认为.
Yes, well, it seems she has reason to believe that Kevin thought...

94
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:13,740
她长得像玩具熊
that she looked like a Gummy Bear.

95
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:17,480
凯文？德国小组的凯文？
Kevin? The one in the German Club?

96
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:19,960
是德国小组的组长
My dear, the chancellor of the German Club.

97
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,760
自从啤酒节派对以来.
Oh, no. She's had a crush on him since--

98
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,700
她一直暗恋他
Yes, since the Oktoberfest polka party.

99
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,060
可怜的孩子，她一定很伤心了
Poor kid. She must be miserable.

100
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:29,460
她回家后我会找她谈谈
Well, I'll talk to her when she gets home.

101
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:31,120
-她没事了 -是吗？
- She's fine now. - She is?

102
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,160
是的，我们谈过，谈妥了
Yeah, we talked it over. Figured it out.

103
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,560
-你？ -是的
- You did. - I did.

104
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:39,585
你这样说只是不想让我愧疚吧？
Honey, you don't have to say that just so I won't feel guilty.

105
00:06:39,585 --> 00:06:41,100
不是的
I'm not, Maggie.

106
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:44,140
我和凯罗谈了个清清楚楚，明明白白
No, we talked the whole thing over through and through, inside and out.

107
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:49,020
哭了，笑了，拥抱了 最后还一起唱歌
We cried. We laughed. We hugged. We closed with a song.

108
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:56,080
杰森，那就太好了 不过我还是会找她谈
That's good, Jason. But if you don't mind, I think I'll talk to her just the same.

109
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:57,500
她没事了
She's fine, Maggie.

110
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,720
亲爱的，她嘴上说说而已
Honey, she always says she's fine.

111
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:00,700
她何时回来？
Now when's she coming home?

112
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:04,360
你认为我要单方面终止协议？
You don't think I can hold up my end of the bargain, do you?

113
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:06,100
什么协议？
Jason, what bargain?

114
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,420
“你工作..”
Come on, the bargain where you go back to work...

115
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:10,120
“我留在家照顾孩子”的协议
and I stay here and take care of the kids.

116
00:07:10,149 --> 00:07:12,225
-杰森 -你认为.
- Oh, Jason. - No. You don't think...

117
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,660
我办不到？
that I can handle it, do you?

118
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:17,180
-杰森，不是我认为.. -尽管我恰好是.
- Jason, it's not that I don't think-- - No, no, no. Even though I happen to be...

119
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:20,700
-一位职业心理医生 -杰森.
- a highly skilled professional counselor... - Oh, Jason.

120
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:23,680
我曾成功劝阻一名跳鲨鱼池的人
... who once talked a man down from the rim of a shark tank.

121
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:26,320
我曾经在警察抓人前两周.
No, no. I mean, because I was the guy...

122
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:29,800
准确预测那名犯人.
who predicted two weeks before the police caught Son of Sam...

123
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:33,260
正是来自新罗谢尔的邮差.
that he would turn out to be an ugly mailman from New Rochelle...

124
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,660
因为他跟邻居的狗说话
who talked to his neighbors dog.

125
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:39,380
我认为你是一名出色的心理医生
Jason, it's not that I don't think that you're a wonderful psychiatrist.

126
00:07:39,778 --> 00:07:42,354
但你不是一名母亲
But you're just not a mother.

127
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:47,520
那就好了，这围裙穿着真不舒服
Well, that's fine with me because this girdle is killing me.

128
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,480
本，爸妈呢？
Hey, Ben. Wheres Mom and Dad?

129
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:10,160
麦克，有何不可告人？
Hey, Mike. What you hiding from them?

130
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,140
我？隐瞒亲爱的妈妈..？
Me? Hide something from my beloved mother and--

131
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:16,960
不!又一只!
Oh, no. Not another one.

132
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:18,600
会咬人吗？
Will it bite me?

133
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:21,300
怎么了本？不认得老朋友斯图了？
What's the matter, Ben? Don't you recognize your old pal, Stuart?

134
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,760
-麦克，斯图是黑色的 -又怎样？
- Mike, Stuart is black. - So?

135
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,920
-这狗是白色的 -那怎样？
- This dog is white. - So?

136
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,600
这是明显的不同
So I think that's a noticeable difference.

137
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,480
你得帮我，斯图跑掉了
Look, Ben. You gotta help me. Stuart ran away.

138
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:35,740
-温蒂定会宰了你 -除非她不知道
- Wendy's going to kill you. - Not if she doesn't find out.

139
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:38,040
麦克，即使是你的女朋友.
Mike, even one of your girlfriends...

140
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:41,020
也有可能记得自己狗的颜色
has a shot at remembering the color of her own dog.

141
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,440
我会应付温蒂的
I'll take care of Wendy.

142
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,540
你确保爸妈不知道就行了
You just make sure Mom and Dad don't find out.

143
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:47,640
大家好
Hi, guys.

144
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:49,760
什么狗？
What dog?

145
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:52,740
-谁说狗了？ -我没有
- Who said anything about a dog? - Not me.

146
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:56,000
-妈妈 -甜心
- Hi, Mom. - Hi, sweetheart.

147
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:57,480
你好吗？
How are you?

148
00:08:57,923 --> 00:09:00,535
很好，时间刚刚好
Fine. Great, just in time for my show.

149
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,700
我收到留言了 要不是整天不在办公室.
I got your message, and I would've called you back...

150
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:04,240
我早就回你电话了
but I was out of the office all day.

151
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:05,280
妈妈，没关系
That's okay, Mom.

152
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,120
瞧那家伙
Look at this guy.

153
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,700
什么节目？
What is this?

154
00:09:09,768 --> 00:09:12,379
<彼得街上的鲟鱼>
The Sturgeons of Pitt Street.

155
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,440
管家干嘛趴在地上？
Why is the butler on all fours?

156
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,580
家里的狗死了，他们不敢告诉婆婆
The family dog died, and they didn't have the heart to tell Grandma.

157
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:24,160
你要谈谈今天在学校的事吗？
So, honey, you wanna talk about what happened at school today?

158
00:09:26,552 --> 00:09:29,265
-凯罗？ -你刚说什么？
- Carol? - Mom, what'd you say?

159
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:31,740
凯文的话一定让你很伤心了
You must be really upset about what Kevin said.

160
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:36,880
广告来了，好
Good. A commercial.

161
00:09:37,930 --> 00:09:39,801
咱聊聊
So lets talk.

162
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,700
这个凯文是怎么了？
What's with this Kevin anyway?

163
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,780
我已经跟爸爸谈过了
I already talked the whole thing through with Dad.

164
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:47,640
也许女人之间的谈话.
I know that, but I thought maybe a woman-to-woman talk....

165
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:49,060
不必了，妈妈，我没事
No, really, Mom. I'm fine.

166
00:09:49,174 --> 00:09:51,716
真的？
You are? You're sure?

167
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:55,820
亲爱的，你不用害怕让我有愧疚感
Honey, you don't have to say that just so that I won't feel guilty.

168
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:58,040
我发誓我没事
No, I swear it's okay, Mom. You know...

169
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:01,040
还以为你回去工作我会不习来惯.
I thought I wasn't gonna like it when you went back to work...

170
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:04,900
现在爸爸在家也挺好的
but it's really kind of neat having Dad at home now.

171
00:10:07,292 --> 00:10:08,800
很好
That's great.

172
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:13,799
那个鲟鱼节目开始没有？
Hey, those wacky Sturgeons on yet?

173
00:10:13,799 --> 00:10:16,535
-爸爸，过来坐中间 -好的
- Come on, Dad. Sit in the middle. - Yeah. Okay.

174
00:10:16,535 --> 00:10:19,350
-妈妈，过去一点 -好的
- Could you move over a little, Mom? - Yeah.

175
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:21,340
很好看的
You're gonna love this.

176
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,120
嗨，我是温蒂
Hi, it's Wendy.

177
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,240
温蒂，进来
Hi, Wendy. Come on in.

178
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,540
-还好吗？ -很好
- How you doing? - Fine.

179
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,400
假期怎样？
How was your vacation?

180
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:43,960
很棒，我们首先去了欧洲 接着去了法国
It was great. First we went to Europe, and then we went to France.

181
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:49,160
你们的旅行社真棒
Yes, well, you must have quite a travel agent.

182
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:54,080
麦克，温蒂来了
Mike, Wendy's here.

183
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,800
斯图没带给你们许多麻烦吧？
I hope Stuart wasn't too much trouble for you.

184
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:58,160
斯图？没有
Stuart? No, no.

185
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:00,880
自从喂它吃邻居的孩子后.
No, no, once we started feeding him the neighbors children...

186
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,020
它好像人间蒸发了
we hardly knew he was here.

187
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:05,460
-温蒂 -麦克
- Hey, Wendy. - Hi, Mike.

188
00:11:05,617 --> 00:11:07,590
嗨，小斯图
Hi, Stuey-pooey.

189
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,580
温蒂，看它见到你后多高兴!
Wow, just look how glad he is to see you, Wendy.

190
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:15,020
真像斯图!
That does look like Stuart, doesn't it?

191
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:16,380
连颜色也一样
Same color and everything.

192
00:11:16,662 --> 00:11:19,680
温蒂，带斯图回家吧
Yes. Wendy, why don't I take you and Stuart home?

193
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:24,060
斯图，来吧，对了，好狗狗
Come on, Stuart. Come on. Yeah, that's it, good dog. Yeah.

194
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,480
温蒂，瞧它.
Just look at him, Wendy. I mean...

195
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,320
知道你要回来，它太兴奋了.
he was so excited about you coming home last night...

196
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:32,760
昨晚彻夜不眠，现在已经精疲力尽
that he didn't sleep a wink. And now, of course, he's exhausted.

197
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:43,320
-本 -爸爸？
- Ben? - Yeah, Dad?

198
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:45,700
麦克对斯图怎样了？
What did Mike do to Stuart?

199
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:50,120
-要说真相？ -是的
- The truth, Dad? - Yeah, Ben.

200
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,460
麦克没对斯图怎么样，再见
Mike didn't do anything to Stuart. Bye, Dad.

201
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,420
-嗨，甜心 -嗨
- Hi, sweetheart. - Hello.

202
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:01,840
-凯罗呢？ -不知道
- Where's Carol? - I don't know.

203
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:05,700
我们要去度假？
Are we going on vacation here?

204
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:10,140
不，我要带凯罗到城里玩
No, no, I just thought I'd take Carol into the city for the day.

205
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:13,180
看看画展.
You know, take in a couple of art galleries...

206
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:14,840
接着去绿色餐馆吃饭
run up to Tavern on the Green for lunch...

207
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:16,920
或者逛逛布朗克斯动物园
and then maybe pop over to the Bronx Zoo.

208
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:21,680
凯罗一定爱看从底特律运来的白色猎狗
I know Carols been dying to see that albino hyena on loan from Detroit.

209
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,000
底特律有这些东西？
Those things come from Detroit?

210
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,540
如果有时间的话.
Anyway, I thought if we had time--

211
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,060
你告诉凯罗了吗？
Listen, sweetheart, does Carol know about all this?

212
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,780
没有，怎么了？
No, why?

213
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:35,980
我今天约了凯罗逛商店.
Well, Carol and I we're planning to go shopping together today...

214
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:36,920
要买溜冰鞋
for a new pair of skates.

215
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,640
这对她来说很重要
I think it's important to her...

216
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:43,020
因为凯文和其它人.
because, well, you know, Kevin and the other kids...

217
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:44,740
今天下午要去溜冰
are all going skating this afternoon.

218
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,980
舞会就在今晚举行
Yes, and you know the big dance is tonight.

219
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,020
-不是吧？ -是的
- No. - Oh, yes.

220
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:52,980
我不知道呢
No, I didn't realize that.

221
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:57,760
那就归你管了
But then that's more your area now.

222
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,820
亲爱的，你俩玩得开心点
Well, honey, you two have a good time.

223
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:05,620
-麦姬，要一起去吗？ -不了，我只会妨碍你们
- Maggie, you want to come with us? - No, I'd just be in the way.

224
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,100
别傻了
No, no. Don't be ridiculous.

225
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,960
我在家也很好玩
No, no, I can have fun here. Really.

226
00:13:10,175 --> 00:13:14,993
洗洗衣服，清洁厕所
I'll just do the laundry, maybe clean a few toilets.

227
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:18,860
你不介意我和凯罗一起吧？
Does it bother you that Carol and I have plans together?

228
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,720
不介意
No. No.

229
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,160
这是好事
I think it's great.

230
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:28,500
她昨晚没空跟我聊
I mean, sure, she didn't have time to talk to me last night...

231
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,380
今天没空陪我
and she doesn't have time to be with me today...

232
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:32,860
我很高兴你俩在一起
but I love seeing the two of you together.

233
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:37,320
你是她爸爸，她是你女儿
You're her father. She's your daughter.

234
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,700
你们是父女，父女应该融洽
You're father and daughter. You should do things together.

235
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,700
做些父女做的事情，我替你们高兴
Father and daughter things. I'm very happy for you.

236
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,460
-麦姬 -怎么了？
- Maggie. - What?

237
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,280
凯罗那天气冲冲放学回来.
You know, when Carol came home from school yesterday all upset...

238
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,040
她真的要找你
she really wanted to talk to you.

239
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:56,180
是的，她死也不肯跟爸爸聊
Oh, yes. it was like pulling teeth to get her to open up to old Dad.

240
00:13:56,721 --> 00:13:58,161
是吗？
Yeah?

241
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,840
她还是需要妈妈的
She still needs her mother, you know.

242
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,140
有时候我感觉不到这点
Sometimes I don't feel like it.

243
00:14:05,660 --> 00:14:06,220
她确实需要你
She does.

244
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,440
家里穿围裙的还是你
And you still wear the girdle in the family.

245
00:14:09,468 --> 00:14:11,612
-是吗？ -而且穿得很漂亮
- Yeah? - And very nicely.

246
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:17,120
你是说我有点过火了？
So you're saying that I'm overreacting a bit.

247
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:20,020
不，我是说你太过火了
No, no, I'm saying you're overreacting a lot.

248
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:28,119
爸爸，这是斯图成长的一个阶段
Dad, I'm telling you it's just a phase that Stuart's going through.

249
00:14:28,119 --> 00:14:30,764
人会改变，狗也一样
I mean, people change, dogs change.

250
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:33,280
你没读过<旅程>吗？
Look, did you ever read Passages?

251
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:42,440
温蒂，怎么了？
Wendy. ?Que pasa? How's it going?

252
00:14:42,667 --> 00:14:45,846
小斯图，怎样了？
Hey, Stuart. How you doing, little fella?

253
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,940
麦克，这不是斯图
Mike, this isn't Stuart.

254
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,940
温蒂，温蒂.
Wendy. Wendy. Wendy.

255
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,340
不是斯图是谁？
Who would this be if it's not Stuart?

256
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:57,320
不知道，这狗湿了会掉色
I don't know, Mike. But this dog changes colors when he gets wet.

257
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,360
斯图不会这样的
Stuart would never do that.

258
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,200
报纸上有篇文章.
You know, theres an article about this in the paper.

259
00:15:03,255 --> 00:15:05,940
说宠物偶尔会改变颜色
They're saying pets are changing colors left and right now.

260
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,020
那是因为酸雨的关系
It's that acid rain, you know.

261
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,780
麦克，瞧瞧
Mike, look.

262
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,860
在辛辛那提有一只髯狗变紫色了
There's a schnauzer in Cincinnati that turned purple.

263
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,140
听说这是完全正常的
They say it's perfectly normal.

264
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:15,080
报纸还在楼上，我去拿
I have the article upstairs. I'll go get it.

265
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,400
麦克，别动
Mike, stop.

266
00:15:18,136 --> 00:15:19,609
坐下
Sit.

267
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:21,940
你对斯图怎样了？
Now what did you do to Stuart?

268
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,780
让它跑掉了
I lost him.

269
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,400
我到处找也找不到
Look, I looked everywhere, but I couldn't find him.

270
00:15:28,813 --> 00:15:32,017
温蒂，原本我要告诉你的
Wendy, I would've told you the truth but...

271
00:15:32,017 --> 00:15:34,161
但是我扪心自问.
then I asked myself:

272
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,820
真相是什么？
What is truth?

273
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,660
是诚实吗？
Is it honesty?

274
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:40,740
还是苦楚？
Or is it pain and grieving?

275
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:45,180
还是姑娘美丽的笑靥？
Or is it the smile on a beautiful girls face?

276
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:49,060
你知道我的答案了吧
I guess you know what I think the truth is.

277
00:15:49,968 --> 00:15:53,443
你弄来一条白狗，染成黑色
Now you took a white dog and you dyed him black.

278
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:56,180
谁要是把一条黑狗托付给我麦克.
Hey, when somebody leaves a black dog with Mike Seaver...

279
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:57,920
谁就能要回一条黑狗!
they get a black dog back.

280
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:02,400
温蒂，真是对不起
Look, Wendy, I'm really sorry about all of this.

281
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,900
你肯定很喜爱斯图了
I know how much you must have loved Stuart.

282
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:09,020
-什么？谁喜爱斯图了？ -什么？
- Are you kidding? Who could love Stuart? - What?

283
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:12,240
我们全家度假就是为了躲开斯图
My family went on vacation to get away from Stuart.

284
00:16:12,591 --> 00:16:14,269
什么？
They what?

285
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:17,960
但是我喜欢这条狗，很温驯
But I love this dog. He's so sweet.

286
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:20,040
我叫它小麦克好了
I think I'll name him Mikey.

287
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:24,260
不，叫它小小麦克
No, make that Mikey-Poo.

288
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,260
爸爸，听到了吧？ 她要叫它小小麦克
Did you hear that, Dad? She's gonna name it Mikey-Poo.

289
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,800
今晚见
I'll see you tonight.

290
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:34,520
-再见 -好的，再见
- Bye. - Yeah, okay. Bye.

291
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:44,780
爸爸，我知道教训了 我以后不敢了
Well, I learned my lesson, Dad. I'll never do that again.

292
00:16:44,789 --> 00:16:46,900
当然了
No, you wont, Mike.

293
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:50,280
因为我要关你一辈子
Because you're grounded for the rest of your life.

294
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:53,100
-爸爸，你..一辈子？ -再加一个月
- Dad, you.... Life? - And a month after that.

295
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,080
麦克怎样了？
What's with Mike?

296
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:04,400
-我要关他一辈子 -又来了？
- I just grounded him for life. - Again?

297
00:17:06,344 --> 00:17:07,960
真是不敢相信
I do not believe it.

298
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,520
亲爱的，怎么了？
Honey, what's wrong?

299
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:13,200
爸爸，你猜玛丽莎说的话
Dad, you're not gonna believe what Melissa told me.

300
00:17:13,251 --> 00:17:14,386
什么？
What?

301
00:17:14,386 --> 00:17:17,998
玛丽莎说马克告诉凯文.
Melissa told me that Mark told Kevin...

302
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:20,760
我经常流汗
that I sweat a lot.

303
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,840
宝贝，我们昨天不是说好了.
Well, sweetheart, didn't we decide yesterday...

304
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,780
玛丽莎的话不大可信吗？
that Melissa's really not that reliable a source?

305
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,620
爸爸，现在一切都不同了
Yeah, but, I mean, everything's different now, Dad.

306
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:31,480
事情一发不可收拾
I mean, the whole thing is blown wide open.

307
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,371
玛丽莎说.
You see, Melissa said that she--

308
00:17:33,371 --> 00:17:37,654
等等，还是让专家来处理吧
Hey, wait. You know, this would be a good one to run by the old pro here.

309
00:17:41,479 --> 00:17:42,952
好
Okay.

310
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:46,180
接着我跟马克聊 他说他从没有那样说
But then I talked to Mark, and he said he never even said that...

311
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,780
玩具熊的事也一样
or the Gummy Bear thing, either.

312
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:48,960
马克，哪个马克？
Mark. Who's Mark?

313
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
接着凯西说她当时在场.
But then Cathy tells me that she was right there...

314
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,125
听到马克告诉凯文我经常流汗
when Mark told Kevin that I do sweat a lot.

315
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:57,480
能告诉我马克是谁吗？ 还有昨天的事.
Honey, if you could just tell me who Mark is and what happened yesterday--

316
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,080
妈妈，这兴昨天无关
Mom, this has nothing to do with how it happened yesterday.

317
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:03,601
问题是不知道玛丽莎和马克 哪个可信
The point is I don't know whether I trust Melissa or Mark...

318
00:18:03,601 --> 00:18:06,246
-因为凯西说.. -等等，宝贝
- cause Cathy says-- - Wait, wait, wait, sweetheart.

319
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:09,960
你说过凯西也喜欢凯文
Now you said that Cathy also had a thing for Kevin.

320
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:13,020
对，那？
Yeah, so?

321
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:16,280
那就是说凯西也不可信
Well, that doesn't make Cathy a very reliable source, either.

322
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:21,840
天哪，这就是说大家都有问题
Oh, God, Dad. You know what this means? This means everybody's in on it.

323
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:25,040
-麦姬，等等 -太不公平了
- Maggie, wait. - Dad, it's just not fair.

324
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:30,528
亲爱的，若是凯文值得你喜欢.
Honey, look, if Kevin is really worth caring for...

325
00:18:30,528 --> 00:18:33,606
他自然会有自己的想法
then he's gonna make up his own mind.

326
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,900
他已经做出选择了
Yeah, well, I guess he already has...

327
00:18:36,568 --> 00:18:39,577
他没有邀请我去舞会
"cause he didn't ask me to the dance.

328
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:54,400
麦姬，别生气 凯罗只是气在头上
Maggie, don't be mad. Carol's just upset.

329
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:58,660
-她没有要排挤你 -我没有生气
- She didn't mean to exclude you. - I am not mad.

330
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:01,100
我只是讨厌那些.
I am just tired of people taking things out of the cabinets...

331
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,680
不把东西放回柜子的人
and not putting them back where they belong.

332
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,040
-你要找什么？ -不知道
- Well, what are you looking for? - I don't know.

333
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:12,080
是不是那瓶1982年吃完的.
Well, on the off-chance that it's the mango chutney...

334
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:13,000
芒果酱？
we finished it in 1982.

335
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,800
麦姬，我理解你的心情
Come on, Maggie. I know what you're feeling.

336
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:22,440
你无法理解我的心情
You do not have any idea what I am feeling, Dr. Seaver.

337
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:23,420
听我说.
Hey, look--

338
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:26,700
你也许理解凯文 马克和玛丽莎的心情.
No, you may know what Kevin, Mark, and Melissa are feeling...

339
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:29,460
但你不理解我的心情
but you do not know what I am feeling.

340
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,660
麦姬，我没有要排挤你
Maggie, I tried to include you--

341
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:34,580
杰森，别客套了
Don't patronize me, Jason.

342
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:37,380
还说我是专家，嗟来之食
Throwing me a bone, calling me an old pro.

343
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:40,420
若干年后 或许在老人节才能让我回来
Maybe in a few years you can bring me back for Old-Timers Day.

344
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,080
我们不是谈过了吗？
We talked about all of this.

345
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:46,500
玩具熊事件暴发时.
I just happened to be the guy who was here...

346
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:49,780
我刚好在家而已
the day the whole Gummy Bear thing exploded in our faces.

347
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:54,540
不单是玩具熊，过去3个月以来
It's not just the Gummy Bears, Jason. It's the whole past three months.

348
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,120
你宠爱孩子的方式.
The way you've been pampering the children.

349
00:19:57,248 --> 00:19:58,580
怎么了？
What?

350
00:19:58,580 --> 00:20:01,240
制作本最爱的巧克力甜饼
Making Bens favorite chocolate chip cookies.

351
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,020
这有什么不对？
What's wrong with that?

352
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,340
“有什么不对”？
"What's wrong with that? "

353
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:07,280
不对的是你把我从孩子的生活中 排挤出去
What's wrong with that is you"re edging me out of my children's lives.

354
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:09,680
排挤出去？这就是你的想法？
Edging you out? Is that what you think?

355
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:13,040
你是专家，不如你说说我的想法
I don't know. You're the expert. Why don't you tell me what I think?

356
00:20:14,165 --> 00:20:15,605
好的
Okay.

357
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:19,180
你因为回去工作而感到愧疚
I think you feel guilty about going back to work.

358
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,620
当然了
Of course I do.

359
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:23,420
你想要我多陪孩子们
And I think you want me to be here to spend time with the kids.

360
00:20:23,420 --> 00:20:24,700
当然了
Of course I do.

361
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:26,720
你想要我善于照顾孩子
And I think you want me to be good at it.

362
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,920
当然了
Of course I do.

363
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:31,380
但这方面我不能超越你
But you don't want me to be as good as you are.

364
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:33,140
当..当然了
Of course I do.

365
00:20:39,090 --> 00:20:40,427
那个.
Well...

366
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,660
也许不是
maybe I don't.

367
00:20:49,334 --> 00:20:52,040
麦姬，在我上班时.
You know, Maggie, I was at work...

368
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:54,660
本踏出了他的第一步
when Ben took his first step...

369
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:59,420
凯罗说出了第一句话
and when Carol spoke her first sentence...

370
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:02,120
还有麦克.
and when Mike...

371
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,020
麦克第一次犯罪
committed his first illegal act.

372
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:10,020
这些我都错过了
I missed out on all that.

373
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:13,060
现在我有机会了.
And now I have the chance...

374
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:16,680
可以更靠近孩子们 花更多时间陪他们
to be closer to the kids, spend more time...

375
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,860
你不高兴？
and you begrudge that?

376
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,732
杰森，不是的，真的.
Oh, Jason, I don't. Really--

377
00:21:20,732 --> 00:21:23,809
也许是的，我也曾有那种感觉
No, maybe you do. I know that feeling, too.

378
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:28,300
逝去的是时光
Because it's time that goes.

379
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,520
一去不复返
And it never comes back.

380
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,540
他们长大了.
They grow up...

381
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,520
叫人伤心
and it hurts.

382
00:21:42,487 --> 00:21:43,857
是的
Yeah.

383
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:45,740
很伤心
It hurts.

384
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:50,020
回去工作感到愧疚吗？
Are you sorry you went back to work?

385
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:52,340
要回家吗？
You want to come home?

386
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,260
不要
No, I don't.

387
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:57,980
我猜.
I guess....

388
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:02,240
我是想拥有全部
I guess I just want to have it all.

389
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:04,711
这是不可能的
But you cant.

390
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:13,580
凯罗呢？
How's Carol?

391
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,560
她不用跟凯文去舞会
Well, she's not going to the dance with Kevin.

392
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:20,480
-太糟糕了 -是的
- Oh, no, that's too bad. - Yeah.

393
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:24,395
但还有另外一个刺激的约会
But she does have a chance at another date that she was pretty excited about.

394
00:22:24,395 --> 00:22:26,440
-真的？约会谁？ -真的
- Really? Really? Who with? - Oh, yeah.

395
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:31,020
不大清楚，她说过是什么白色猎狗
I don't know exactly, but she said something about an albino hyena.

396
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,840
-底特律那些？ -但不是底特律原产
- From Detroit? - Yeah. Well, not originally, no.

397
00:22:37,342 --> 00:22:40,590
救命，斯图回来了!
Help! Stuart's back!

398
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:52,380
管家怎么躺着了？
Why is the butler lying on his back?

399
00:22:52,890 --> 00:22:54,933
他在装死
He's playing dead.

400
00:22:56,620 --> 00:22:58,300
婆婆怎么躺着？
Why is Grandma lying on her back?

401
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,440
她死了
She is dead.

402
00:23:01,899 --> 00:23:04,306
<鲟鱼>真是个怪节目
Oh, those wacky Sturgeons.

403
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:07,100
瞧，都死光光了
Look, they're all dead.

404
00:23:51,196 --> 00:23:52,185
Thanks for watching [zeroxia@gmail.com] 2006.03.12
